$\alpha=\sqrt3+1\approx 2.732$:

* $\alpha^2=4+2\sqrt3\approx 7.464$, fractional part $\approx0.464=1-\beta^2$;
* $\alpha^3=10+6\sqrt3\approx 20.392$, fractional part $\approx0.392=\beta^3$;
* $\alpha^{10}\approx 23167.956$, fractional part $\approx 0.956$;
* $\alpha^{11}\approx 63296.032$, fractional part $\approx 0.032$.

The values alternate between being close to $1$ and close to $0$, as proved above, so there is no limit.
